type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135489952,imgsize-148122.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[US appeals court upholds $114,663 legal fee award, ruling AI use alone does not prove overbilling]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135508298.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[A federal appeals court recently upheld the award of $114,663.11 in legal fees, rejecting claims related to AI usage. The court clarified that accusations of inflated billing require concrete evidence, particularly following Flux Drive Inc.'s unsuccessful trade-secrets lawsuit. This ruling reinforces the notion that simply employing AI does not warrant a reduction in legal fees, establishing a significant precedent for similar cases moving forward.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/a-us-company-argued-that-lawyers-using-artificial-intelligence-should-receive-lower-fees-after-its-trade-secrets-lawsuit-was-dismissed-a-federal-appeals-court-has-upheld-a-114663-award-saying-no-overbilling-was-shown/articleshow/135508298.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/a-us-company-argued-that-lawyers-using-artificial-intelligence-should-receive-lower-fees-after-its-trade-secrets-lawsuit-was-dismissed-a-federal-appeals-court-has-upheld-a-114663-award-saying-no-overbilling-was-shown/articleshow/135508298.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-03T23:01:20+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135508556,imgsize-109244.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Blue wave, Red resilience or gridlock? Three ways US midterms could play out]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135507084.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[As election day for the US midterms arrives, the atmosphere is charged with anticipation. Three distinct scenarios could shape the future of Congress: a sweeping Democratic wave may bring notable victories, whereas a slim Democratic majority may present hurdles in legislation. On the flip side, Republicans retaining control over both chambers could steer Trump's political agenda. The results await, holding the potential to influence the nation significantly.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/us-mid-term-elections/news/democratic-wave-republican-resilience-or-gridlock-three-ways-us-midterms-could-play-out/articleshow/135507084.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/us-mid-term-elections/news/democratic-wave-republican-resilience-or-gridlock-three-ways-us-midterms-could-play-out/articleshow/135507084.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-03T22:35:37+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135507590,imgsize-97587.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA['We won't be paying Israel': Trump says $4 billion funding to stop end of the year]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135507321.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/we-wont-be-paying-israel-trump-says-4-billion-funding-to-stop-end-of-the-year/articleshow/135507321.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/we-wont-be-paying-israel-trump-says-4-billion-funding-to-stop-end-of-the-year/articleshow/135507321.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-03T22:28:37+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Prisha Patnaik</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-13